    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Fibrates cut TG by about 50% and raise HDL-C by up to 20%; trials showed ⍉benefit from adding a fibrate to a statin."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Fibrates potentiate warfarin. Fenofibrate may be the safest fibrate to use w a statin."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Fenofibrate tablets, severe hypertriglyceridemia: 54–160 mg QD, adjusted by repeat lipids every 4–8 wk (max 160 mg). Mild–mod renal impairment: start 54 mg/day. Stop if ⍉adequate response after two months @ 160 mg."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Fenofibrate:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ALT, AST and bili @ baseline and periodically; stop w liver-injury signs or persistent enzyme elevation. It can reversibly raise creatinine: check renal funct periodically in renal impairment."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
